Subject: Research output that misled an assistant

Found in the assistant tool review of the live gateway (2026-10-28):

- edhrec_commander wrote "8 sorcerys": the plural is now spelled per type.
- edhrec_recommendations: EDHREC scored all ten suggestions 100, so the
  score ranked nothing; it suggested "Mountain"; and with four cards given,
  "Consider Cutting" listed all four, Sol Ring and Goblin Warchief among
  them, which an assistant read as advice to cut staples. Basic lands are
  now left out (and counted), a score is shown only when the scores differ,
  and with fewer than 20 cards given no cut list is shown (a sentence says
  why); a longer cut list says to check each card first.
- spellbook_combos and spellbook_card_combos printed Commander Spellbook's
  steps as one run of text while its own text says "Repeat step 4": the
  steps are numbered now. Mana needed and Prerequisites are always listed,
  "none" when Spellbook sends none, so every combo has the same lines.
- edhrec_combos lists the most played combos first (EDHREC's page order is
  not by deck count).
- edhrec_top_cards sorts a section by deck count when every card carries
  one (the lands page sent Forest before Mountain), and says "Period
  ignored" only when a period was passed with a color.
- edhrec_precon_upgrade lists the first 10 commanders (and the one shown)
  and says how many more, and explains that each card's share is of the
  decks that could play it, so the totals differ from card to card.
- precon_search says "1 result" and gives each deck's release year.

tests/test_research_wording.py; tests/test_research_output_fixes.py gives a
whole deck's worth of cards to its cut-list test.

Upstream: Kautiontape/mystic-forge at dd82cd1 has none of these. Needs
patches 0001-0013 applied first.

